# arch-replay-cursor.cases — the case inputs both halves read, one CASE record per line.
#
# CASE|<case-id>|<restart>|<basis>|<rows>|<reader-cursor>
#
# The frozen trace is four task rows the implementation wrote. `restart` is `none` for a plain open
# and `checkpoint` for an open that writes a projection checkpoint and then reopens the same root.
# `basis` names the policy basis the reopening supplies: `same` is the issuing policy, `changed`
# differs in one run-lineage field, `missing` supplies none. `rows` is how many frozen rows the root
# holds. reader-cursor is a consumer that has read through seq 1.
CASE|cursor-live|none|same|4|1
CASE|cursor-after-restart-same-basis|checkpoint|same|4|1
CASE|cursor-after-restart-changed-basis|checkpoint|changed|4|1
CASE|cursor-after-restart-missing-basis|checkpoint|missing|4|1
